urname>Kaczmarek</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Querze</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Zardi</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The fibronectin isoform containing the ED-B oncofetal domain: a marker of angiogenesis</article-title><source>Int J Cancer</source><year>1994</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>612</fpage><lpage>618</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7525495</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zardi</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Carnemolla</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Siri</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Petersen</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name><name><surname>Paolella</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Sebastio</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Baralle</surname><given-names>FE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transformed human cells produce a new fibronectin isoform by preferential alternative splicing of a previously unobserved exon</article-title><source>Embo J</source><year>1987</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>2337</fpage><lpage>2342</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2822387</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carnemolla</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Borsi</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Bannikov</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Troyanovsky</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Zardi</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of human tenascin expression in normal, simian-virus-40-transformed and tumor-derived cell lines</article-title><source>Eur J Biochem</source><year>1992</yea